I was punished (although I was not quite that misbehaving :-). When passing
by a rockmole it did do something quite nasty. I had the heavy iron ball
in my knapsack, but the iron chain was on the floor. The rockmole wanted
to eat (?) the iron chain and the next thing I know the dungeon collapsed.
The panic stated that the error was in "freeobj". I think this is more
or less what happend, because I did not take too much notice of all messages.
As a matter of fact, I was running away from some other monsters, when the
rockmole entered the room and grabbed the chain.
Has anyone seen this before ? If so: what should I do to prevent it ?
If not: can/should it be patched ?

I have the save file of this crash but what should I do with it ?
Is there a way to deal with it ? Is there a way to store the last
messages in a normal readable ascii file, that is: the same messages which
you can retrieve with the ^P commands ? This could reveal more information
as it shows part of the history. At least non-NetHack guru's may be able
to read what they were doing (wrong).

Oops almost forgot: as I was dying under the collapsed dungeon, NetHack still
wanted me to show the stuff I was carrying. This didn't work anymore
(i.e. nothing was shown), so probably the inventory list was broken.
It also left my terminal in the wrong mode, e.g. no echoing.
